# Gotcha entry — template

> Copy the block below into a consumer project's `AGENTS.md` §8 Gotchas OR into
> its personal add-on (e.g. `consumer-d.md`). One bullet per gotcha, ordered newest
> first. Do NOT batch multiple gotchas into one line.

## Public gotcha (goes in AGENTS.md §8 — team devs see it)

```markdown
- {{YYYY-MM-DD}} — **{{one-sentence headline}}**. {{1-3 sentence detail covering
  what to avoid, what to do instead, and how you discovered it}}. See
  [{{trace or link}}]({{url or path}}).
```

### Example

```markdown
- 2026-04-23 — **NestJS `@ApiOperation` missing on DELETE endpoints breaks MCP
  tool discovery.** Missing decorators cause the `consumer-c-api` MCP server
  to skip the route; agents see fewer tools than expected. Always decorate
  with `summary` + `description` (ADR-002). Caught by Acceptance Auditor on
  change `module-1-ingredients-implementation`. See
  [openspec/changes/module-1-ingredients-implementation/retros/2026-04-23.md](...).
```

---

## Personal gotcha (goes in consumer-d.md / add-on — Arturo-only)

Same shape, but add a `[personal]` tag so the deprecation watcher can tell the
two apart in monthly retros:

```markdown
- {{YYYY-MM-DD}} [personal] — **{{one-sentence headline}}**. {{detail}}.
```

### Example

```markdown
- 2026-04-23 [personal] — **LiteLLM restart loops Hindsight even when
  Hindsight itself is healthy.** Always `curl localhost:4000/health/liveliness`
  first; if LiteLLM is down, Hindsight embeddings cannot resolve and it crash
  loops. Mentioned in `docs/operations/consumer-d-stack-troubleshooting.md`
  (March 2026 incident).
```

